    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass. The feature is fully implemented and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation from an optional request `birthDate`, computed against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `birthDate` (ISO `date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema (request/round-trip) and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` with the new field and `AgeBandEnum`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, so a supplied birth date survives to the `GET` read-back.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `birth_date DATE` column to the owners table in the hsqldb, h2, mysql, and postgres `schema.sql` files, and appended the corresponding `NULL` to the positional seed inserts in hsqldb `data.sql` (h2/postgres use column-named inserts, so no change needed there).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", \u2026)` with an `ageBand(owner)` helper: it returns `null` when `birthDate`/`registrationDate` is absent, otherwise computes full years via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)` \u2192 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+). MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` on both directions since the names match.\n\nThe request `birthDate` flows through the existing `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner` pipeline unchanged (no new function class needed \u2014 it's a plain field), and the band is derived on the response like the other computed owner fields. `Cp34Tests` and all 47 tests pass.",
